  "summary": "I am an IT Professional who has a wide range of experience from racking/cabling systems to designing an environment supporting IBM’s Government Regulated Data lab (HIPAA, FFIEC, SPI, etc) and development of an internal cloud solution. Throughout my career I believe I have been acquiring the skills necessary in building a firm base of technical expertise. I’ve demonstrated success in design of Windows/Linux environments, automation to reduce manual task and increase productivity, staff supervision, fulfillment of internal/external customer needs, and software development. Recognized for high level of self-learning, building strong customer relationships, breadth of technical ability, and advance troubleshooting skills.\n\nSkills\n- Virtualization (VMware & KVM)\n- Operating Systems (Windows Server and Linux - Ubuntu/Red Hat)\n- Networking concepts and network services (VLAN, Subnetting, NAT, DHCP, DNS, etc.)\n- Distributed storage using Ceph - providing scalable block and file\n- Automation/Scripting - PHP, Python, Bash, etc.\n- Database (MariaDB) and SQL Queries\n- Programming & Version Control - APIs, PHP, Python, GitHub, etc.\n- Security Hardening - ModSecurity, Fail2Ban, CIS-CAT benchmarks, and security best practices\n- IBM Entry/Mid-Range/Enterprise Storage (V7000, XIV, & SVC) Data-At-Rest Encryption (FIPS140-2 Level 3) with redundant central key management using Gemalto KeySecure appliances.\n- Cisco MDS SAN & Brocade Encryption Switches\n- Cisco Nexus and FEX Networking\n- High Availability solutions using Microsoft Failover Clustering\n- Microsoft Active Directory",
